In https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/master/test/test_jit.py#L5900-L5945 there are several methods with multiple return statements like below:
@torch.jit.script_method
def forward(self, x):
    x = self.conv(x)
    return x
    x = self.bn(x)
    return F.relu(x, inplace=True)
It seems they are redundant, as subsequent return statements are unreachable. If they are there for a debugging purpose, a comment would be nice.

🚀 Feature
For distributions created by calling torch.distributions.Independent, support covariance_matrix
Motivation
This will make it easier to treat multivariate distributions in a uniform way. Of course, this covariance matrix will just be a diagonal of the variance of (batched) distribution that was used to create the Independent distribution.
Pitch
I think the implementation is just something like the following. (I guess this only works when reinterpreted_batch_ndims==1.)
@lazy_property
def covariance_matrix(self):
    return tt.diag(self.base_dist.variance))

